You are debugging a production issue involving an asynchronous order processing pipeline. Under load, operations inside `enrichAndPersist()` fail to access the authenticated user's credentials, and database mutations fail to roll back when an exception occurs inside `persistOrder()`.

java
@Service
public class OrderService {

    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Order> processOrder(Order order) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> enrichAndPersist(order))
            .thenApply(this::notifyCustomer);
    }

    private Order enrichAndPersist(Order order) {
        // Relies on SecurityContextHolder and local database transaction
        User user = SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication().getPrincipal();
        return persistOrder(order, user);
    }

    private Order notifyCustomer(Order order) { ... }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an API aggregator executes multiple downstream microservice calls concurrently. When any single downstream service experiences network latency or fails, the entire application's custom thread pool becomes saturated, causing cascading request timeouts across the entire platform.

java
public List<Response> fetchAggregatedData(List<ServiceTask> tasks, ExecutorService customExecutor) {
    List<CompletableFuture<Response>> futures = tasks.stream()
        .map(task -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(task::callExternalService, customExecutor))
        .toList();

    CompletableFuture<Void> allOf = CompletableFuture.allOf(
        futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])
    );

    allOf.join();

    return futures.stream()
        .map(CompletableFuture::join)
        .toList();
}
